.TH ROCKET-RUN-MODULE 1 "November 2026" "iree-rocket" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rocket-run-module \- run one function of a rocket-compiler module on the RK3588 NPU
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rocket-run-module
[\fB\-\-cpu\-only\fR]
[\fB\-\-cpu\-ids=\fILIST\fR | \fB\-\-iree\-cpus\fR]
[\fB\-\-iterations=\fIN\fR]
.I MODULE.vmfb FUNCTION
[\fIINPUT\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Loads
.I MODULE.vmfb
(as produced by
.BR rocket-compiler (1))
into a libiree_rocket_runtime session over the Rocket NPU and CPU devices
together, calls
.I FUNCTION
(for example
.BR module.main_graph )
with the given inputs, and prints each result the way
.BR iree-rocket-run-module (1)
prints it, so the two can be compared.
.PP
Each
.I INPUT
is in IREE's text form, for example
.BR 1x3x224x224xf32=0.1 .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-cpu\-only
Use only the CPU device. Runs modules compiled without NPU work, and works on
machines with no NPU.
.TP
.BI \-\-cpu\-ids= LIST
Pin the CPU workers to these CPUs, for example
.BR 4\-7 .
The default is the fastest CPU cluster.
.TP
.B \-\-iree\-cpus
Use IREE's own worker placement instead.
.TP
.BI \-\-iterations= N
Call the function
.I N
times. The time of the first call, and the mean of the rest, go to standard
error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /dev/accel/accel0
The NPU, through the mainline rocket kernel driver. Opening it needs read and
write access, which Debian gives the
.B render
group.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rocket-compiler (1),
.BR iree-rocket-run-module (1),
.BR iree-rocket-benchmark-module (1)
